from pathlib import Path
import json
# Invented training scenarios, not claims about events in the series.
rows = [
('Abstraction','Naruto','Imagine Kakashi saying “begin the drill” instead of explaining every foot placement and hand movement.','One high-level command hides the lower-level steps; the steps still happen.'),
('Virtualization','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine a training room that makes each student feel they have a private arena, while a coordinator alternates their turns in one real arena.','The apparent private resource differs from the shared physical resource. This is an imagined training setup, not a claim about domain mechanics.'),
('Kernel / privilege','Demon Slayer','Imagine a training compound where only authorized instructors may unlock the weapon store. Trainees must request access.','Privileged operations require trusted authority; ordinary work does not grant that authority.'),
('System call / supervisor call','Naruto','Imagine a ninja filling out a mission request, then handing it through the Hokage office’s designated service window.','Preparing the request is the wrapper; the controlled entry into the office is the supervisor call. A normal conversation is not a privilege change.'),
('Interrupt / trap','Demon Slayer','Imagine an outside messenger interrupting Tanjiro’s drill, versus the instructor stopping him because of the move he just performed.','The external message resembles an interrupt; the current action triggering intervention resembles a trap.'),
('Shell','Naruto','Imagine giving a mission coordinator a written sequence: gather supplies, assemble the team, then depart.','The coordinator interprets commands, like a shell; the coordinator is not the entire village administration.'),
('Multiprogramming','Demon Slayer','Imagine Tanjiro waiting for equipment while Zenitsu uses the training floor.','Another ready task uses the available resource during someone else’s wait; waiting time need not leave the CPU idle.'),
('Time-sharing','Naruto','Imagine Naruto and Sakura alternating timed turns at one training dummy even when neither has finished practicing.','Enforced turns resemble preemption and time slices; they do not create extra physical dummies.'),
('CPU-bound / I/O-bound','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine one student spending nearly the entire drill performing moves, while another repeatedly waits for equipment to arrive.','Doing the moves represents CPU work; waiting for an external service represents I/O waiting.'),
('Byte / word','Demon Slayer','Imagine supply beads bundled eight at a time, then placed into boxes whose capacity is specified by the training camp.','The eight-bit bundle is a byte; the machine-defined box is a word. Word size must be given, not assumed.'),
('Environments','Naruto','Imagine a village archive optimizing bulk paperwork, a messenger station optimizing quick replies, and a defense post meeting strict warning deadlines.','Different missions imply different optimization goals, just as OS environments prioritize throughput, response, or deadlines.'),
('Evolution','Demon Slayer','Imagine a growing training camp: one instructor first handles everything, then adds queues, rotating stations, personal kits, and communication between camps.','This is a memory aid for increasing coordination needs, not the literal history of computers. Learn the hardware-generation mapping from the definition.'),
('SaaS','Naruto','Imagine ordering a finished meal at a village restaurant: you use the result without managing the kitchen.','You consume the completed application; the provider operates what makes it run.'),
('PaaS','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine designing your own drill in a school-run arena where staff maintain the floor, lighting, and equipment systems.','You supply the application while the provider maintains its execution platform.'),
('IaaS','Demon Slayer','Imagine renting an empty training hall and equipment, then choosing and maintaining the camp’s procedures yourself.','The provider supplies infrastructure; you take responsibility for the guest OS and application layers.'),
('Open source','Naruto','Imagine a training scroll whose license permits studying, adapting, and sharing it. A scroll displayed behind glass grants only viewing.','Readable instructions alone are not enough: the permissions to modify and redistribute matter.'),
('Process / program','Naruto','Imagine one written training routine practiced independently by Naruto and Sakura, each at a different step with separate supplies.','The routine is the program; each active practice is a process with its own state.'),
('Ready / running / blocked','Demon Slayer','Imagine three trainees: one awaits a free floor, one practices on it, and one cannot proceed until a replacement sword arrives.','They are ready, running, and blocked respectively. A free floor cannot help the trainee still missing equipment.'),
('Context switch','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine pausing Yuji’s drill, recording his current step and setup, then restoring Megumi’s saved drill setup.','Save the outgoing execution state before restoring the incoming one; switching is more than changing a name on a roster.'),
('New / suspended / terminated','Naruto','Imagine missions awaiting admission, missions put on administrative hold, and completed missions retained for a debrief.','These differ from waiting for a resource; a suspended task needs explicit reactivation.'),
('Virtual CPU benefits','Demon Slayer','Imagine the same training plan running in a camp with one shared floor or several floors, with coordinators managing the difference.','The plan can remain independent of physical resource count; fewer floors may still mean slower completion.'),
('PCB','Naruto','Imagine a mission dossier recording the ninja’s current step, status, supplies, priority, and which mission launched it.','The PCB is the structured record of one process, not the process’s executable instructions.'),
('TCB','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine a shared team mission with an individual bookmark and action log for each student.','Each thread needs its own control state while team-wide resources remain shared.'),
('Sibling representation','Naruto','Imagine a team leader’s record naming the first recruit, while each recruit records the immediately earlier and later recruit.','Parent, first-child, and adjacent-sibling links reconstruct the hierarchy without a separately allocated child-list node for every relationship.'),
('Array vs pointers','Demon Slayer','Imagine reserving a full equipment locker for every possible trainee versus reserving a small label and acquiring a locker only when needed.','Fixed records reserve space upfront; pointers to dynamically allocated records add allocation work but avoid reserving every full record.'),
('RCB','Demon Slayer','Imagine a sword-rack ledger showing whether a particular practice sword is available and who is waiting for it.','An RCB records the resource and its waiters; a PCB records the process and what it owns.'),
('Request','Naruto','Imagine Naruto requesting a training dummy already reserved by Sakura. He joins its queue while keeping his other supplies.','A failed request can block the caller without automatically releasing resources it already holds.'),
('Release','Demon Slayer','Imagine Tanjiro returning the only practice sword and the attendant assigning it to the first waiting trainee.','Ownership transfers and the waiter becomes ready; that does not guarantee immediate CPU service.'),
('Ready list convention','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine the instructor’s eligible roster includes both the student currently on the floor and students awaiting their turns.','That matches the course RL convention. A blocked student waiting for equipment is on a different list.'),
('Shared thread data','Naruto','Imagine a team sharing one mission map and supply room, while each teammate keeps an individual action log.','Shared map and supplies resemble shared process data/resources; individual logs resemble private stacks and register state. Real threads are not isolated copies.'),
('User-level threads','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine a student coordinator dividing a team into subgroups, but the school recognizes only one team admission pass. If that pass is held up, all subgroups wait.','In many-to-one mapping, the kernel sees one execution stream; a blocking call can stall all user threads mapped to it.'),
('Kernel-level threads','Demon Slayer','Imagine camp staff tracking each trainee individually and assigning them to separate available training floors.','Kernel-visible threads can be scheduled independently, subject to the available CPUs.'),
('Pointer / pointee','Naruto','Imagine two notes both giving the location of the same scroll. Changing the scroll affects what either note leads you to; changing one note’s address does not change the other.','The notes are pointers and the scroll is the pointee. Copying an address creates an alias, not another scroll.'),
('Thread completion','Demon Slayer','Imagine Tanjiro lending teammates written instructions, then waiting for them to return before erasing the instructions or combining their reports.','Join before reclaiming argument storage or relying on completed results; launching work does not mean it has finished.'),
('Long-term / short-term','Naruto','Imagine the village first admitting missions into today’s workload, then deciding which admitted mission gets the next available squad.','Admission is long-term scheduling; selecting among runnable work is short-term scheduling.'),
('Preemptive / nonpreemptive','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine an instructor either stopping an ongoing drill for another student or allowing it to continue until it finishes or must wait.','The difference is whether runnable work can be displaced before it voluntarily stops.'),
('FCFS (FIFO)','Demon Slayer','Imagine trainees using a practice station in arrival order, each keeping it until done.','Arrival order sets service order; a short drill behind a long drill still waits.'),
('SJF (SJN)','Naruto','Imagine Kakashi picking the shortest predicted next drill among students already waiting, without interrupting the current student.','Compare the predicted next CPU bursts only when choosing a new job; a later short arrival does not preempt the current job.'),
('SRT','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine an instructor always choosing the drill with the least work still unfinished, even stopping a longer drill when a shorter one arrives.','Compare remaining work, not original length or time spent waiting. A previously long job may now be almost finished.'),
('Starvation','Demon Slayer','Imagine a trainee with a long drill always being passed over as new short drills arrive. Everyone else progresses, but that trainee never starts.','This is indefinite postponement, not necessarily a group trapped in circular waiting.'),
('Quantum Q','Naruto','Imagine an instructor giving each ninja a maximum of two minutes on a shared dummy before rotating the queue.','The quantum is a service limit, not the task’s total requirement. Finishing early releases the station early.'),
('Multilevel (ML)','Demon Slayer','Imagine separate priority lines at a training camp, with fair turns inside each line but service always taken from the highest nonempty line.','Fairness within one queue does not guarantee that lower-priority queues ever run.'),
('Multilevel feedback (MLF)','Naruto','Imagine each new drill getting one minute first; unfinished drills then move to queues with two-minute and four-minute turns.','The queue responds to observed CPU use. The course doubles the time allotment as priority falls.'),
('Two-tier / floating priority','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine urgent response drills above routine training, with returning students receiving a temporary boost based on why they were waiting.','Separate the fixed high tier from behavior-based priority. An event boost is added to base priority, not accumulated blindly on the current value.'),
('Period / deadline','Demon Slayer','Imagine a guard reporting every ten minutes, with each report required before the next reporting interval ends.','Ten minutes is the period; each particular report has its own absolute deadline.'),
('Rate monotonic (RM)','Naruto','Imagine recurring patrol reports every four and seven minutes. The four-minute report always gets higher priority.','RM ranks by the fixed period, regardless of which individual job currently has the nearer absolute deadline.'),
('Earliest deadline first (EDF)','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine two training reports due at 10:05 and 10:08. The earlier due report takes priority, even if its usual reporting cycle is longer.','EDF ranks the deadlines of currently pending jobs, so priorities can change between releases.'),
('Feasible schedule','Demon Slayer','Imagine a defense drill where every warning must reach its station before its assigned cutoff. Finishing most warnings quickly is not enough.','All deadlines must be met; averages and CPU utilization alone are not the definition of feasibility.'),
('Race condition','Naruto','Imagine Naruto and Sakura both reading “10 supplies,” independently adding their deliveries, then each replacing the ledger total. The last entry can erase the other delivery.','A read-modify-write sequence can lose an update when interleaved; source-code appearance does not make it atomic.'),
('Critical section','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine the short procedure that edits the school’s shared equipment ledger while everyone else must wait to edit it.','The critical section is the code performing the protected access, not the ledger object itself.'),
('Mutual exclusion','Demon Slayer','Imagine a single editing token for the training roster: only its holder may change the roster.','At most one conflicting editor enters at a time. This alone does not guarantee fairness or that required data exists.'),
('Lockout prevention','Naruto','Imagine Naruto cannot train because the roster insists it is Sakura’s turn, although Sakura is not trying to train.','An uninterested participant must not prevent an interested one from entering an available critical section.'),
('Deadlock / starvation','Demon Slayer','Imagine two trainees each holding one tool and waiting for the other’s tool; compare that with one trainee repeatedly losing every equipment allocation.','The first is circular waiting with no progress; the second is starvation while others can continue.'),
('Priority inversion / inheritance','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine an urgent mission waiting for a junior student’s locked equipment box, while routine drills keep delaying that student. Temporarily let the student finish first.','Boost the lock owner so it can release the needed resource; do not let the urgent task bypass mutual exclusion.'),
('Abstract P / V','Naruto','Imagine three training passes. Taking a pass before entering is P; returning a pass is V. With no pass available, the next ninja waits.','Permits represent available capacity. Taking or returning must be indivisible relative to competing operations.'),
('Signed internal count','Demon Slayer','Imagine an equipment board where +2 means two spare passes and −2 records two waiting trainees rather than negative physical swords.','A negative internal semaphore value represents queued demand; it is not the abstract number of usable permits.'),
('Mutex-style semaphore','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine exactly one token for updating a shared mission board. Take it before editing and return it once afterward.','Initialize to one and balance acquire/release. Fair access requires an appropriate admission policy as well.'),
('Busy waiting','Naruto','Imagine Naruto repeatedly asking “is the dummy free?” instead of waiting to be called while another trainee finishes.','Polling consumes execution time without advancing the waiting task; blocking lets other runnable work use that time.'),
('Lost wakeup','Demon Slayer','Imagine the attendant calling “your sword is ready” just before a trainee joins the waiting line. The trainee then waits for a call that already happened.','Registration and sleeping must coordinate with notification so the wakeup cannot fall into the gap.'),
('Monitor','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine an equipment office whose inventory can be changed only through its counter, serving one transaction at a time with a separate waiting area.','Encapsulation controls access; mutual exclusion protects operations; condition waiting frees the counter for someone else.'),
('Condition wait','Naruto','Imagine stepping away from the mission counter to wait for a missing document, allowing other ninjas to use the counter.','A condition wait relinquishes monitor ownership while blocking; it does not consume a stored semaphore permit.'),
('Condition signal','Demon Slayer','Imagine an attendant calling the next trainee in a waiting line. If nobody is waiting, that call is not saved as a ticket for a future arrival.','A condition signal has no accumulated credit; a later waiter still needs the predicate and proper notification protocol.'),
('Hoare-style signal','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine a clerk immediately handing the counter to a waiting student when their equipment arrives, while the clerk waits in a priority return line.','The waiter runs immediately and the signaler waits urgently. Only one participant remains inside the monitor at a time.'),
('Mesa / Java-style notification','Naruto','Imagine Kakashi announcing that a station may be available, then finishing his current task. By the time Naruto gets access, someone may have changed the situation.','A notified waiter reacquires the lock and rechecks the predicate in a while loop; notification is not a reservation.'),
('Priority wait','Demon Slayer','Imagine trainees setting wake-up times and the attendant sorting the requests by those times instead of arrival order.','The condition queue uses an explicit priority. Equal-time waiters may all need release during the same tick.'),
('Readers-writers','Naruto','Imagine several ninjas reading a mission scroll together, but a scribe needing exclusive access to revise it. New readers pause when a writer is waiting.','Concurrent reads are compatible; writes exclude readers and other writers. The course additionally batches waiting readers after a writer finishes.'),
('Dining philosophers','Demon Slayer','Imagine five trainees in a circle, each needing both adjacent practice tools. If everyone grabs only the left tool, they can all wait forever.','Multiple resources create circular-wait risk. A solution should also allow nonadjacent trainees to practice together.'),
('Monitor test(i)','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine five training stations in a ring. A waiting student can activate a station only when neither neighboring station is active; finishing prompts checks of both neighbors.','Test the requesting state and both neighbors atomically. Merely being hungry or waiting does not grant access.'),
('Elevator algorithm','Naruto','Imagine a messenger moving upward through a tower, delivering pending scrolls in floor order, then reversing at the highest requested floor.','Sweep in the current direction, then reverse when no requests remain ahead. Count travel from the messenger’s starting floor too.')
]
rows.extend([
('Thread','Naruto','Imagine several ninjas working on one mission. Each follows a separate set of steps while sharing the team’s scrolls and supplies.','The mission is the process; each execution path is a thread with its own place in the instructions.'),
('Round Robin (RR)','Demon Slayer','Imagine trainees taking turns at one practice station. Each gets a fixed interval, then moves to the back of the line if more practice is needed.','The interval is the quantum. A finished trainee leaves the queue, and one waiting for equipment does not keep the station.'),
('Concurrency','Jujutsu Kaisen','Imagine two students progressing through drills by alternating turns in one training arena. Both drills advance during the same afternoon.','Overlapping progress does not require simultaneous execution; one CPU can alternate between tasks.'),
('Parallelism','Naruto','Imagine two ninjas practicing at separate stations at the same moment.','Separate processing units allow instructions from different tasks to execute simultaneously.')
])
assert len(rows)==73
out={front:{'series':series,'story':story,'connection':connection} for front,series,story,connection in rows}
assert len(out)==73
(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'analogies.js').write_text('/* Original, hypothetical anime training analogies; technical definitions remain authoritative. */\nwindow.FLASH_ANALOGIES = '+json.dumps(out,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+';\n')
